Testing: Gates

Purpose:
  Defines testing gates including unit, integration, E2E, UI, and manual QA.

TestGates:
  UnitGate:
    Format: UNIT-GATE-<ID>
    Condition: All unit tests pass
    Evidence: test result
    Threshold: Failed = 0
    Owner: QA/Developer

  IntegrationGate:
    Format: INTEGRATION-GATE-<ID>
    Condition: All integration tests pass with real dependencies
    Evidence: test result
    Threshold: Failed = 0
    Owner: QA/Developer
    Dependencies:
      - API
      - DB
      - Redis
      - Queue

  E2EGate:
    Format: E2E-GATE-<ID>
    Condition: All E2E tests pass
    Evidence: test result
    Threshold: Failed = 0
    Owner: QA
    Layers:
      - FE → API → BE → DB
      - MD → API → BE

  UIGate:
    Format: UI-GATE-<ID>
    Condition: UI tests pass
    Tools:
      - Playwright
      - Cypress
      - Detox
      - Flutter integration
    Owner: QA

  ManualQAGate:
    Format: MANUAL-QA-GATE-<ID>
    Condition: Manual test passed
    Evidence: manual test result
    Threshold: PASS / FAIL / BLOCKED
    Owner: QA

TestGateRules:
  [TG1]  Unit tests MUST pass before integration tests.
  [TG2]  Integration tests MUST pass before E2E tests.
  [TG3]  E2E tests MUST pass before release.
  [TG4]  UI tests use stack-appropriate tools from skill registry.
  [TG5]  Manual QA results MUST be recorded in graph.

State: +
  